# Examples Policy

Code examples in framework rules are illustrative.

They demonstrate preferred and discouraged patterns, but they are not mandatory implementation templates.

Do not copy example names, paths, classes, methods, roles, users, endpoints, tags, or domains unless they already exist in the project.

Adapt the pattern to the actual project map and existing architecture.

Follow the architectural intent of the example, not its exact naming or domain.

If an example conflicts with the project map, existing framework structure, or dedicated project rules, follow the project map and the more specific rule.

Do not create new abstractions only because they appear in an example.